--TEST--
`clone` of an array is refused — ADR 0023 § 1 makes it a new instance of the operand's class, and an array names none
--FILE--
<?nvs
// An `array<T>` is already copied when it is assigned (ADR 0004's
// copy-on-write), so this is not a missing feature: there is nothing for
// `clone` to do that the assignment on the line below does not already do.
array<int> $a = [1, 2, 3];
array<int> $b = clone $a;
echo Core\Arr::count($b), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0781]: `clone` makes a new instance of a class, and `array<int>` is not an object
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
